 is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9\\,\\text{ft},\\,w=4\\,\\text{ft},\\,h=5\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=9\\cdot 4\\cdot 5=180\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540072 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a97dc9e3-b5a4-5913-94c3-aea43e639ce8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Volume and Some Other Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8d9721dd-9208-5ac3-8341-cca0a666f5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539720} {:answer/id #uuid "9709a9e9-4f71-5997-92f0-59b28c00158f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539730} {:answer/id #uuid "9abb1b20-1580-55d3-b002-2fb5704a0832" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539736} {:answer/id #uuid "a90cee9c-478e-5ec6-a1f5-d3e5a0596142" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539766} {:answer/id #uuid "c7dc03a9-ee66-57a2-ba71-d566f83336b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539824}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d9721dd-9208-5ac3-8341-cca0a666f5f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539720} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8a913b0-6cc8-5fe3-b6f8-11eba32fd2c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91cc3a07-1501-5243-8832-8d928c7de8f2" :question/math-academy-id "q-107620" :question/problem "![](images/ab/abec41d02ba71b2e94d7b2c3cd92f552ddab907de494719a22706b568a588be4.png)\n\nDetermine the length of the rectangular solid above given that its volume is $84\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nV=84,\\,w=3\\sqrt{2},\\,h=\\sqrt{8}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}84 & =l\\cdot 3\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{8} \\\\ 84 & =3\\sqrt{16}l \\\\ 84 & =12l \\\\ l & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is $7\\,\\text{cm}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540047 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41a556a7-74b8-5f77-8473-47998a47590d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,280\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539599} {:answer/id #uuid "c4120e78-7ffa-5428-886a-a8780dc4f9de" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "19\\,760\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539817} {:answer/id #uuid "ccada324-ead9-51a5-afcc-0e4711ff3f76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,800\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539830} {:answer/id #uuid "d197ef72-bbca-5188-bd5b-b8ee0acc0017" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15\\,840\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539839} {:answer/id #uuid "d9117a9a-638d-54bf-ba34-918349539f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,480\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539851}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "41a556a7-74b8-5f77-8473-47998a47590d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "17\\,280\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539599} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ed7cb6-b944-5862-8ee4-2c83a098bcf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539951}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3e2801a7-e084-5269-a941-751cceb06faf" :question/math-academy-id "q-107630" :question/problem "A storage center has ten identical storage units in the form of a rectangular solid. Each unit is $9\\,\\text{ft}$ long, $24\\,\\text{ft}$ wide, and $8\\,\\text{ft}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the units?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one storage unit.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=24,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 24\\cdot 8=1\\,728\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the ten storage units is\n\n$$\n1\\,728\\cdot 10=17\\,280\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540022 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1925be10-596c-557e-b94e-7843f3e27ddf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$47.72$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539530} {:answer/id #uuid "2c6bbdb9-99c3-511d-98b5-292b6419acef" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$49.95$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539562} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a0135e-96f1-5953-b50e-81d6419a564b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$57.42$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539781} {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2dbc0-3274-5cf1-8bab-4898a8a2fd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$54.88$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539812} {:answer/id #uuid "f17db65a-f656-5936-ad46-cb4b659e7dad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$50.25$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539884}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0a2dbc0-3274-5cf1-8bab-4898a8a2fd18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$54.88$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539812} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab997a9e-66ed-5632-8075-dc62b6beef15" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "014f97dd-12f1-54e9-8347-3c53a77026ab" :question/math-academy-id "q-107731" :question/problem "![](images/62/6240abf268497f82475003619689d979b0b00678b4d49972ff2fbcf1fa866a9c.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows a cubic gas tank. One-fifth of the volume of the tank is filled with gas. If the fuel costs $$0.0016$ per cubic centimeter, how much would it cost to fill the tank to capacity?" :question/worked-solution "The length of $7\\,\\text{cm}$ shown in the diagram represents one-fifth of the tank's side length. Therefore, the length of each side of the tank is\n\n$$\n5\\cdot 7=35\\,\\text{cm}.\n$$\n\nThe empty space in the cube is a rectangular prism that is $35\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $35\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $35-7=28\\,\\text{cm}$ high.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=35\\,\\text{cm},\\,w=35\\,\\text{cm},\\,h=28\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=35\\cdot 35\\cdot 28=34\\,300\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, to fill the tank to capacity, it would cost\n\n$$\n34\\,300\\cdot 0.0016=$54.88.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "94e026db-b6ca-5d1f-bc3c-3be6b14dd14a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1.80$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116735} {:answer/id #uuid "aaf356cf-15b6-5092-9788-e98b4f596935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$8.50$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116736} {:answer/id #uuid "d22f8719-b0f3-5d7a-8f03-f8cb18846173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116737} {:answer/id #uuid "f581f57c-328a-511b-adf3-7882b27f3560" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.02$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116738} {:answer/id #uuid "35dc34cf-6ed5-588b-8665-51cdf9e08eda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$6.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d22f8719-b0f3-5d7a-8f03-f8cb18846173" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$7.20$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116737} :answer-field/id #uuid "8e3ac18f-df2a-531e-80f1-3bbd339896a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186116734}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f9fb6d92-70dd-5c7f-9979-070fe590bd5f" :question/math-academy-id "q-107738" :question/problem "A bar of chocolate in the form of a rectangular prism is $9\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $5\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $2\\,\\text{cm}$ high. If the chocolate costs $$0.02$ per cubic centimeter, what is the value of four identical bars of chocolate?" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of the bar of chocolate.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=9,\\,w=5,\\,h=2\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=9\\cdot 5\\cdot 2=90\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe total volume of the four bars of chocolate is\n\n$$\n90\\cdot 4=360\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the cost of four chocolate bars is\n\n$$\n360\\cdot 0.02=$7.20.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540030 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d503d5d-ee8f-57a2-a6ef-b5b05d5e8ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "65ca4abc-8804-5fe2-b1c7-ad9e9b7405cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539647} {:answer/id #uuid "a6bd20fd-c6db-51c6-a437-4bdcbcd94cfd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539759} {:answer/id #uuid "b5db93b5-d18a-5e67-97d5-1d26114ac9bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539796} {:answer/id #uuid "b6614c90-73d8-59d1-b9a8-ec416c37740a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539798} {:answer/id #uuid "d690fe31-c203-5665-a0e4-a2b44d77bd60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539846}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6614c90-73d8-59d1-b9a8-ec416c37740a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539798} :answer-field/id #uuid "0f2203bf-6439-554d-8839-4b779c975b9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539926}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e1eb62e-08d0-56cd-999d-56094605f117" :question/math-academy-id "q-118846" :question/problem "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{ft},$ $\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft},$ and $2\\,\\text{ft},$ respectively?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{ft},\\,w=\\sqrt{10}\\,\\text{ft},\\,h=2\\,\\text{ft}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=\\sqrt{5}\\cdot \\sqrt{10}\\cdot 2=2\\sqrt{50}=10\\sqrt{2}\\,{\\text{ft}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540088 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119890 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d503d5d-ee8f-57a2-a6ef-b5b05d5e8ae4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3fbb90ef-bc77-5686-9580-446faecd9e3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539593} {:answer/id #uuid "7f7f4592-9da2-5474-a594-ba6a8d8c4cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539690} {:answer/id #uuid "89b6545b-5746-51bf-aca8-6f1e543c301e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539710} {:answer/id #uuid "f738c182-3c34-5f58-9454-a452628c6586" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539896} {:answer/id #uuid "fec1133d-d1fa-5ad9-a094-ba9d15c6621c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7f7f4592-9da2-5474-a594-ba6a8d8c4cbe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "70\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539690} :answer-field/id #uuid "c9b4e360-8590-5911-8f82-2ddfc942a0b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539997}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bc3873ba-541e-5572-9cfe-0e10d2402ed6" :question/math-academy-id "q-118847" :question/problem "What is the volume of a rectangular solid that has length, width, and height of $7\\,\\text{cm},$ $\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm},$ and $2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm},$ respectively?" :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=7\\,\\text{cm},\\,w=\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm},\\,h=2\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain\n\n$$\nV=7\\cdot \\sqrt{5}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5}=14\\sqrt{25}=70\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540064 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a97dc9e3-b5a4-5913-94c3-aea43e639ce8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Volume and Some Other Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e2e2ed-aed5-5203-a591-0631b899ac63" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539492} {:answer/id #uuid "2b8af707-5ffc-56b6-b779-92eaa5dc63aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539557} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4e1721-1eb0-5dfe-a24f-dc033aec8da7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539620} {:answer/id #uuid "9cc7fd52-09a9-5439-9621-e9bed86e9431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539737} {:answer/id #uuid "ee949a8d-6d43-5d32-b575-97cfcab50d2d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9cc7fd52-09a9-5439-9621-e9bed86e9431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539737} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee07a34b-76bb-5c4b-82db-1a6944f98c6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "78b1f6d8-2df3-5686-9ee0-696c5e38afe8" :question/math-academy-id "q-118851" :question/problem "The height of a rectangular solid is $2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}$ and its volume is $24\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.$ If the base  (length × width) of the solid is a square, find the length of the solid." :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSince the base of the rectangular solid is a square, we have that \n\n$$\nl=w.\n$$\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nV=24\\sqrt{3},\\,h=2\\sqrt{3},\\,w=l\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =lwh \\\\ V & ={l}^{2}h \\\\ 24\\sqrt{3} & ={l}^{2}\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ {l}^{2} & =12 \\\\ l & =2\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is $2\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{m}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04a735cc-2bb5-57f8-afb8-bf8a9f6cfe7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,400\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539487} {:answer/id #uuid "253a500f-10a7-5a2b-9a1d-48a97e3d0acb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "720\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539552} {:answer/id #uuid "2db94192-9608-59d6-be5f-b026801ae9ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,040\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539564} {:answer/id #uuid "a7c962e9-6e8e-5b95-b1f4-d86b14823f96" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539762} {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf501-4a8b-53d9-ba1c-97b7ebf0dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539827}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb4cf501-4a8b-53d9-ba1c-97b7ebf0dc55" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539827} :answer-field/id #uuid "60d097f1-bd2b-5eac-9e0c-c6fa3b7f0885" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "90edfdf5-24c3-54cd-8862-63c978f95f47" :question/math-academy-id "q-118872" :question/problem "A person has seven identical boxes in the form of a rectangular solid. Each box is $10\\,\\text{in}$ long, $8\\,\\text{in}$ wide, and $8\\,\\text{in}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the boxes?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one box.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=10,\\,w=8,\\,h=8\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=10\\cdot 8\\cdot 8=640\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the seven storage boxes is\n\n$$\n640\\cdot 7=4\\,480\\,{\\text{in}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186540102 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119892 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ba5bf1d9-f6e2-5494-91fd-31c20d7fa09b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Volume of a Rectangular Solid: Word Problems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15b438ae-a475-5594-ad18-73d79bb97fd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539523} {:answer/id #uuid "3aa5ef76-016b-5b8c-a1bf-7bbd48e16bf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\,400\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539587} {:answer/id #uuid "3c929f1b-223c-53e1-a752-772c1da2087e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539590} {:answer/id #uuid "4161ce64-ccaa-5a03-9428-ac5e7b833fc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539598} {:answer/id #uuid "ca2f13e7-3f99-5d2e-8c4c-1840ccbbf980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539825}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ca2f13e7-3f99-5d2e-8c4c-1840ccbbf980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539825} :answer-field/id #uuid "187877f5-c38d-5e21-86e6-44ed4b5fbfcc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539930}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e195bf20-65ce-5bd5-85a8-c18879f5cecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-118873" :question/problem "A shipping company delivered six identical packages in the form of a rectangular prism. Each package is $40\\,\\text{cm}$ long, $20\\,\\text{cm}$ wide, and $10\\,\\text{cm}$ high. What is the total combined volume of the packages?" :question/worked-solution "First, we need to find the volume of one package.\n\nWe can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nl=40,\\,w=20,\\,h=10\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V=40\\cdot 20\\cdot 10=8\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the total volume of the six packages is\n\n$$\n8\\,000\\cdot 6=48\\,000\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120174 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119891 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a97dc9e3-b5a4-5913-94c3-aea43e639ce8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Dimension of a Rectangular Solid Given Its Volume and Some Other Dimensions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c00bdfc-7553-5b8a-9994-e88f4b109a32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539504} {:answer/id #uuid "2a2ed6a0-1263-58cb-824d-1b8aba422512" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539556} {:answer/id #uuid "7817568b-5170-5238-8a2f-a1349a4c027e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539680} {:answer/id #uuid "cdc461e4-747e-5e77-a24e-b19010b9d344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539833} {:answer/id #uuid "dd28a32c-2749-5e10-9cfd-4d0c0a86a6f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{15}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539858}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdc461e4-747e-5e77-a24e-b19010b9d344" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186539833} :answer-field/id #uuid "04e52b2a-816d-5323-9fac-d9c962ec137e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117205}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b4974d95-bce3-5ff7-8461-630c37925bee" :question/math-academy-id "q-32206" :question/problem "The height of a rectangular solid is $15\\,\\text{cm}$ and its volume is $675\\,{\\text{cm}}^{3}.$ If the base of the solid is a square, find the length of the solid." :question/worked-solution "We can find the volume $V$ of the rectangular prism using the formula\n\n$$\nV=lwh,\n$$\n\nwhere $l$ is the length, $w$ is the width, and $h$ is the height of the solid.\n\nSince the base of the rectangular solid is a square, we have that \n\n$$\nl=w.\n$$\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nV=675,\\,h=15,\\,w=l\n$$\n\ninto the formula, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =lwh \\\\ V & ={l}^{2}h \\\\ 675 & ={l}^{2}\\cdot 15 \\\\ {l}^{2} & =45 \\\\ l & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the length is $3\\sqrt{5}\\,\\text{cm}.$"}]}
